  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Mansoor Ahmed Khan vs The Sr Police Inspector And Anr on 1 November, 2023 Author: M. S. Karnik Bench: M. S. Karnik 2023:Bhc-As:33042 Darshan Patil 930-ba-3392-23.doc In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Bail Application No. 3392 Of 2023 Mansoor Ahmed Khan ..Applicant Vs. The Sr. Police Inspector And Anr. ..Respondents ------------ Adv. Mateen Shaikh a/w Adv. Arshad Shaikh a/w Adv. Razique Shaikh a/w Adv. Muskan Shaikh for the Applicant. Ms. Rutuja Ambekar, App for the State. ------------ Coram : M. S. Karnik, J. Date : November 01, 2023 P.C. : 1. Heard learned counsel for the applicant and learned App for the State. 2. This is an application for bail in respect of the offence punishable under Sections 328, 188, 272, 273 and 34 of the Indian Penal Code (hereafter 'Ipc' for short) and Sections 26(2)(i), 27(2)(e), 23(1), 26(2)(iv) and 30(2)(a) of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006, registered on 04/10/2023 vide C.R. No.155 of 2023 with Kasa Police Mansoor Ahmed Khan vs The Sr Police Inspector And Anr on 1 November, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/119947033/ 1 Station, Palghar. 3 . The applicant is alleged to be the purchaser of tobacco 1/3 Darshan Patil 930-ba-3392-23.doc and gutkha products, transportation and purchase of which is alleged to be an offence under Section 328 of IPC read with other provisions.",
    "facts": "This is an application for bail in respect of the offence punishable under Sections 328, 188, 272, 273 and 34 of the Indian Penal Code (hereafter 'Ipc' for short) and Sections 26(2)(i), 27(2)(e), 23(1), 26(2)(iv) and 30(2)(a) of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006, registered on 04/10/2023 vide C.R. No.155 of 2023 with Kasa Police Mansoor Ahmed Khan vs The Sr Police Inspector And Anr on 1 November, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/119947033/ 1 Station, Palghar. 3 . The applicant is alleged to be the purchaser of tobacco 1/3 Darshan Patil 930-ba-3392-23.doc and gutkha products, transportation and purchase of which is alleged to be an offence under Section 328 of IPC read with other provisions. Except for offence under Section 328 of IPC, all other offences are bailable. Accused Nos. 1 and 2 who were transporting the contraband in a Swift Desire car have been enlarged on bail by this Court. 4. Learned APP opposed the application. 5. The entire contraband has been recovered. The question whether Section 328 of IPC will apply to the alleged offence of the present nature is pending consideration before the Hon'ble Supreme Court. The applicant was arrested on 07/10/2023.",
